('Stripe variables','Production checkout requires a live STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, a configured STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET beginning whsec_, and a valid production site URL. Do not use live keys for automated tests. The application refuses unsafe/missing production checkout configuration. Bank transfer follows its own database/account readiness checks rather than requiring Stripe.'),
('Email and address variables','Configure email in Club Settings and/or the supported server environment. Current code supports SMTP/Brevo and Resend, including SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS or RESEND_API_KEY, plus CLUB_FROM_EMAIL/CLUB_FROM_NAME and optional reply-to settings. Inspect lib/email.ts for precedence. NZ Post address lookup uses server-side NZPOST_CLIENT_ID and NZPOST_CLIENT_SECRET. Do not store secret values in downloadable documentation.'),
('Admin authentication','Create/reuse the Supabase Auth account and its active profile with the minimum appropriate role. Admin routes perform server-side checks, not just sidebar hiding. Inactivity expiry is 10 minutes with activity renewal and a signed server cookie. Profile settings edit name/phone; password change requires the current password and a subsequent fresh login. Check redirect URLs use the production origin rather than localhost.'),
('Data boundaries','Use the service client only after appropriate authorisation or narrowly validated public operations. Public entries/Excel export contain safe paid-confirmed player fields; never expose DOB, contact details, payment identifiers or consent snapshots. Documentation PDFs are public static assets even though the admin menu links to them.'),
