('Configure bank accounts','After the bank migration, add the real account through Admin > Payment Accounts; mark Active and choose membership and/or tournament defaults. Only one active default is allowed for each type. A tournament-specific account overrides the default. Multiple unselected accounts are not guessed. Store actual bank details only in the database. Assigned accounts are protected from deletion; deactivate or reassign deliberately.'),
('Pending state and public visibility','A bank registration uses server-calculated fees and a saved bank account snapshot plus unique M/T-prefixed reference. It returns instructions on screen and in the acknowledgement email without creating Stripe Checkout. Payment/registration stays pending until verified. A tentative tournament registration does not reserve a place. Public confirmed lists and received-payment charts exclude pending entries.'),
('Audited confirmation','Only Admin/Super Admin may approve an offline receipt, with method, 5-500 character note and full-payment acknowledgement. Database operations record the receipt and approver atomically and handle repeated approvals without another receipt. Tournament approval checks capacity and an already confirmed player. A linked completed Stripe payment must be verified as Stripe, not overwritten as cash; an open unpaid session is expired before offline approval where applicable.'),
('Recovery and scope','A failed membership activation can be retried from the existing bank confirmation. Never request a second payment because an email failed. For duplicates, verify the full refund and reconcile the correct registration while keeping the valid paid entry. No automatic bank-feed matching is implemented. The existing separate membership renewal checkout remains Stripe-based; new member bank registration does not change renewal fulfillment.'),
